    {
      "id": "585c7790ffaf42462220",
      "title_original": "Trump open to summit with Xi and Putin — to discuss denuclearization",
      "title_ko": "트럼프, 시진핑·푸틴과 정상회담 열어 비핵화 논의",
      "description": "President Trump wants to hold a trilateral summit with Chinese President Xi and Russian President Putin in China next month to discuss \"denuclearization\" — but not necessarily Ukraine. Why it matters: Such a summit between the leaders of the U.S., China and Russia would be unprecedented. Trump has been talking for two years about his aspiration to reach a deal with Russia and China to reduce the number of nuclear weapons. But so far Putin and Xi haven't shown much openness to the idea. Driving the news: Trump is expected to travel to China in mid-November to participate in the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) leaders' meeting in the city of Shenzhen. The Kremlin has been floating the idea of holding such a meeting since July. Putin raised the issue in two phone calls with Trump, including one last week. The Chinese government hasn't expressed willingness to hold such a summit. What he's saying: When asked on Monday whether such a summit could discuss ending the war in Ukraine, Trump said he wants to hold such a trilateral meeting, but in order to discuss other issues. \"I would do it, not so much for Ukraine, we would have it to talk about denuclearization,\" he said.",
      "source": "Axios",
      "link": "https://www.axios.com/2026/10/19/trump-summit-xi-putin-denuclearization-ukraine",
